From 35a78a7d08da3e4ccd544c13fb63d37b73bdb1a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:15:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(control-plane): enable the scheduler when an
 inventory is set

The control plane never injected a scheduler, so every resource that
needs accelerators stopped at SchedulerUnavailable. When
FORGEMESH_INVENTORY_FILE is set, the lifespan now loads the inventory
and gives the controller's reconciler a FirstFitScheduler over it. The
file is loaded right after the authenticator and before the database
is opened, so an unreadable or invalid inventory makes startup fail
without creating the database, as an invalid API key file does.
Without the variable nothing changes.

The app still has no workflow runtime, so the reconciler reports
WorkflowRuntimeUnavailable before it allocates anything; the workflow
runtime and the launchers follow in later changes. The compose smoke
script comment no longer claims that the repository has no scheduler.
